agentCannotRegister.title = You cannot register for CBAM with this account
agentCannotRegister.heading = You cannot register for CBAM with this account
agentCannotRegister.p1 = You signed in with an agent services account.
agentCannotRegister.p2 = Your client must register for CBAM using their own account.
agentCannotRegister.p3 = After they’ve registered, you can manage their CBAM account by:
agentCannotRegister.bullet1 = signing in to agent services (opens in new tab)
agentCannotRegister.bullet2 = requesting authorisation to manage your client's CBAM returns
agentCannotRegister.p4 = Find out more about:
agentCannotRegister.bullet3 = using an agent services account (opens in new tab)
agentCannotRegister.bullet4 = who must register for CBAM (opens in new tab)

cannotRegisterIndividual.title = You cannot register for CBAM with an individual account
cannotRegisterIndividual.heading = You cannot register for CBAM with an individual account
cannotRegisterIndividual.p1 = You’ve signed in with an individual account.
cannotRegisterIndividual.p2 = To register your organisation for CBAM, sign in using your organisation’s account details.
cannotRegisterIndividual.link = Find out who must register for CBAM (opens in new tab)

assistantCannotRegister.title = You must be an administrator to register for CBAM
assistantCannotRegister.heading = You must be an administrator to register for CBAM
assistantCannotRegister.p1 = You’re signed in with an organisation account that does not have administrator access. Only an administrator can register your organisation for CBAM.
assistantCannotRegister.p2 = Ask your organisation’s administrator to register for CBAM or give you administrator access so you can register.

alreadyRegistered.title = Your organisation is already registered for CBAM
alreadyRegistered.heading = Your organisation is already registered for CBAM
alreadyRegistered.p = You can manage your CBAM obligations in your CBAM account.
alreadyRegistered.button = Go to CBAM account

liabilityIntroduction.title = We need to work out the date your liability for CBAM started
liabilityIntroduction.heading = We need to work out the date your liability for CBAM started
liabilityIntroduction.p1 = We’ll ask you a few questions to work out when you became liable to register.
liabilityIntroduction.p2 = Your liability to register for CBAM starts on one of these dates:
liabilityIntroduction.bullet1 = when you first expected to import CBAM goods worth £50,000 or more into the UK in the next 30 days
liabilityIntroduction.bullet2 = when you imported CBAM goods worth £50,000 or more into the UK in the past 12 months, as assessed on the first day of each month
liabilityIntroduction.p3 = If both scenarios apply, your liability to register for CBAM starts on the earlier date.
liabilityIntroduction.linkText = Find out more about when liability to register for CBAM starts (opens in new tab)
